>   UNNAMED BUT REFERRED-TO EFFORTS ARE STILL PROJECTS. If the document repeatedly refers to an operation, programme, exercise or initiative as a definite thing ("the operation", "the covert UAP operation", "the investigation", "the programme") without ever giving its official name, emit ONE project node for it under a short descriptive name built from actor + purpose + place/period, e.g. "Central Intelligence Agency (CIA) high-altitude balloon reconnaissance programme (1950s)" or "Royal Australian Air Force unidentified-object reporting effort (1970s)". A recurring unnamed effort is the thing the document is ABOUT; leaving it out strands every claim about it on generic nodes.
